# Pre-cached static audio for the consent/gating screens.

This directory is intended for short, pre-rendered WAV files the consent
screen prefers in LIVE mode so the first spoken disclosure is instant and
does not consume the shared Gnani TTS quota each session.

At MVP / demo time these files do NOT exist yet — the consent screen falls
back to the existing server `/api/tts` path and/or browser speech. When you
generate them (see the note below), place them here and the consent hook will
start preferring them automatically in live mode.

GENERATION NOTE (do this once, offline, with your own Gnani credentials):

    python - <<'PY'
    import base64, json, wave, io
    import httpx

    key = ""  # paste your own GNANI_API_KEY from Gnani dashboard — do NOT commit
    url = "https://api.vachana.ai/api/v1/tts/sse"
    payload = {
        "text": "This is an AI assistant assisting you.",
        "voice": "Kaveri",
        "model": "timbre-v3.0",
        "language": "en-IN",
        "speed": 1.0,
        "audio_config": {
            "sample_rate": 48000,
            "num_channels": 1,
            "sample_width": 2,
            "encoding": "linear_pcm",
            "container": "raw",
        },
    }
    headers = {"X-API-Key-ID": key, "Content-Type": "application/json"}
    pcm = b""
    with httpx.stream("POST", url, json=payload, headers=headers, timeout=40) as r:
        for line in r.iter_lines():
            if line is None:
                continue
            line = line.strip()
            if not line or not line.startswith("data:"):
                continue
            obj = json.loads(line[len("data:"):])
            b64 = obj.get("audio")
            if b64:
                pcm += base64.b64decode(b64)
    with wave.open("web/public/audio/consent-en.wav", "wb") as w:
        w.setnchannels(1); w.setsampwidth(2); w.setframerate(48000)
        w.writeframes(pcm)
    print("wrote web/public/audio/consent-en.wav")
    PY

Once the file exists, the consent hook in `web/src/hooks/useSpeak.js` will
prefer it in live mode and fall back to the existing server TTS / browser
speech otherwise. Keep these files short (a single disclosure sentence) so
they are cheap to cache and safe to ship to the client.
